# AI Automation Agency Website

This plan covers the design and implementation of a landing page for an AI Automation Agency featuring a strict Red and Black design aesthetic. We will use plain HTML, CSS (Vanilla), and JavaScript to achieve a premium, high-performance web experience with rich micro-animations.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Please review the proposed approach. Let me know if you would like to add any specific sections (e.g., Services, Testimonials, Contact Form) or if you want to use a framework like React/Next.js/Vite instead of Vanilla HTML/CSS.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend Implementation
The website will be created natively in a new directory: `C:\Users\Mudassir\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\ai-agency-website`.

#### [NEW] `index.html`
Will contain the semantic HTML structure of the page including:
- **Hero Section:** Impactful headline with a call-to-action (CTA).
- **About Us:** Mission Statement focused on AI and Automation.
- **Services Section:** Highlighting offerings like AI Chatbots, Workflow Automation, and Data Analytics.
- **Contact Section:** A sleek contact form for prospective clients.

#### [NEW] `styles.css`
Will contain the styling to achieve a premium aesthetic:
- **Palette:** Deep black background (`#050505`) with striking crimson red accents (`#e60000`, `#ff1a1a`).
- **Typography:** Modern styling using Google Fonts (e.g., 'Inter' or 'Outfit').
- **Effects:** Glassmorphism for services cards to give a futuristic, high-tech vibe.
- **Animations:** CSS transitions and keyframe animations for dynamic interactions (e.g., hovering, scrolling).

#### [NEW] `script.js`
Will contain client-side logic:
- Scroll-triggered reveal animations (elements fade in and slide up as you scroll).
- Dynamic cursor or interactive elements.
- Smooth scrolling for navigation links.

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
- I will run a local web server to visually verify the frontend UI.
- I will ensure the deep red-and-black design feels cohesive, premium, and well-animated.
- I will provide a final walkthrough artifact so you can see the result.
